WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:01.363
Jim.

00:00:02.163 --> 00:00:02.996
Jim

00:00:02.996 --> 00:00:03.996
There we go.

00:00:05.962 --> 00:00:06.795
So surly.

00:00:07.003 --> 00:00:07.836
- Yeah!

00:00:08.343 --> 00:00:10.093
- He needs a whiskey.

00:00:10.344 --> 00:00:11.511
[Upbeat Music]

00:00:14.587 --> 00:00:18.778
So, I just got off an email
thread with Caitlin and Ella

00:00:18.778 --> 00:00:20.559
in L.A. from Buzzfeed.

00:00:20.559 --> 00:00:23.016
They suggested that I
do a video with Rachelle

00:00:23.016 --> 00:00:27.058
where I take her to a really
romantic spot in Paris,

00:00:27.058 --> 00:00:28.745
show her the time of her life.

00:00:28.745 --> 00:00:30.779
I've just been traveling
around Europe for work

00:00:30.779 --> 00:00:33.545
for a few weeks, and I
haven't really spent much time

00:00:33.545 --> 00:00:34.378
with Rachelle.

00:00:34.378 --> 00:00:36.649
We should have a few days
where it's just the two of us

00:00:36.649 --> 00:00:38.489
and do something super romantic.

00:00:38.489 --> 00:00:42.461
But then, because I'm just
like born a cheeky bastard,

00:00:42.461 --> 00:00:45.155
I can't help but want to mess with this.

00:00:45.155 --> 00:00:49.382
And do something that's
genuinely going to surprise her.

00:00:49.382 --> 00:00:52.506
And her dad is over in Scotland right now.

00:00:52.506 --> 00:00:54.155
They haven't seen each other for awhile.

00:00:54.155 --> 00:00:55.992
Rachelle loves all things whiskey.

00:00:55.992 --> 00:00:57.488
She's an absolute expert.

00:00:57.488 --> 00:01:00.969
Her brain is like a catalog
of every whiskey imaginable.

00:01:00.969 --> 00:01:02.938
Maybe we should go to the isle of Arran,

00:01:02.938 --> 00:01:05.034
because we've always said we've wanted to.

00:01:05.034 --> 00:01:07.233
It's finally sunny in
Scotland, which is rare.

00:01:07.233 --> 00:01:09.889
So, let's take advantage
of the weather right now.

00:01:09.889 --> 00:01:12.466
It's affordable. We're living
in London at the moment,

00:01:12.466 --> 00:01:14.521
so it's super cheap and super close.

00:01:14.521 --> 00:01:16.464
Plus, we get to hangout with her family.

00:01:16.464 --> 00:01:18.513
I think that this is something

00:01:18.513 --> 00:01:23.096
that she's gonna really
remember and, hopefully, value.

00:01:25.825 --> 00:01:28.027
Rachelle's putting makeup on right now,

00:01:28.027 --> 00:01:30.547
thinking that we're going to Paris.

00:01:30.547 --> 00:01:35.381
Although I'm lying right now,
it's lying with a good cause.

00:01:35.381 --> 00:01:38.381
I'm so nervous, because I never lie.

00:01:38.445 --> 00:01:39.278
Hey, Rachelle?

00:01:39.278 --> 00:01:40.111
- [Rachelle] Yeah.

00:01:40.111 --> 00:01:42.528
- You excited about our trip?

00:01:42.717 --> 00:01:43.708
- [Rachelle] Yeah!

00:01:43.708 --> 00:01:44.824
- Yeah! Me too.

00:01:44.824 --> 00:01:46.982
- [Rachelle] So stoked to eat some cheese.

00:01:46.982 --> 00:01:49.015
[Tania] How long has it been
since you've gone to Paris?

00:01:49.015 --> 00:01:49.848
- I think about a year.

00:01:49.848 --> 00:01:51.160
- [Tania] What are you most excited about?

00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:54.056
- Eating. You sit on the side
of the road, you look out,

00:01:54.056 --> 00:01:55.139
people watch.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.632
- Finally, we have some
quality time together.

00:01:57.632 --> 00:01:58.465
- Yeah!

00:01:58.666 --> 00:02:01.712
- In the most romantic city in the world.

00:02:01.712 --> 00:02:02.984
Say bye to the house.

00:02:02.984 --> 00:02:05.234
- Bye, house. See you soon.

00:02:06.347 --> 00:02:07.364
- There's a vibrator on the floor.

00:02:07.364 --> 00:02:08.197
- Yeah.

00:02:08.606 --> 00:02:10.375
- [Tania] It's pretty
early isn't it, baby?

00:02:10.375 --> 00:02:12.542
- So early in the morning.

00:02:12.752 --> 00:02:13.919
[Upbeat Music]

00:02:21.268 --> 00:02:25.569
Here we're walking to check
in. She still doesn't know.

00:02:25.569 --> 00:02:26.402
Rachelle?

00:02:26.402 --> 00:02:27.235
- Yes?

00:02:27.235 --> 00:02:31.568
- If you weren't going to
Paris, would you be upset?

00:02:32.238 --> 00:02:33.495
Come here for a sec.

00:02:33.495 --> 00:02:35.053
We're still going somewhere.

00:02:35.053 --> 00:02:37.303
- Okay. Where are we going?

00:02:37.357 --> 00:02:40.274
- Well, you know how I was working,

00:02:40.541 --> 00:02:42.709
and we weren't hanging out for awhile.

00:02:42.709 --> 00:02:44.063
We have a few days off.

00:02:44.063 --> 00:02:44.896
- Yes.

00:02:44.896 --> 00:02:46.053
- And we really wanted
to take advantage of it

00:02:46.053 --> 00:02:47.269
and do something romantic.

00:02:47.269 --> 00:02:48.621
- And go to Paris.

00:02:48.621 --> 00:02:52.121
- Yeah, but I thought that's very generic.

00:02:52.633 --> 00:02:57.133
So, instead, I lied, and I
got us tickets to Scotland.

00:02:57.687 --> 00:03:00.032
I thought maybe we could see your dad.

00:03:00.032 --> 00:03:02.256
And go to some whiskey distilleries.

00:03:02.256 --> 00:03:07.089
And just do something that,
like, you actually really love

00:03:08.915 --> 00:03:09.748
and enjoy.

00:03:09.748 --> 00:03:10.581
- Yeah!

00:03:10.581 --> 00:03:11.414
So, we're not going to Paris?

00:03:11.414 --> 00:03:12.247
- No.

00:03:12.247 --> 00:03:13.080
- Are you mad?

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:16.535
- No! No, I'm excited. I just didn't know!

00:03:16.535 --> 00:03:18.618
- I think this is more...

00:03:21.023 --> 00:03:21.856
you.

00:03:22.511 --> 00:03:24.178
But maybe I'm wrong.

00:03:24.592 --> 00:03:26.175
- No, it is. It is.

00:03:27.354 --> 00:03:28.521
It's exciting.

00:03:28.962 --> 00:03:31.129
We'll get to see Scotland.

00:03:31.187 --> 00:03:32.728
- Yeah, and your family home.

00:03:32.728 --> 00:03:33.895
- And the fam.

00:03:34.045 --> 00:03:35.538
- I brought my turtleneck.

00:03:35.538 --> 00:03:38.263
Because I was trying to be French.

00:03:38.263 --> 00:03:40.601
- Baby, you can be French in Scotland.

00:03:40.601 --> 00:03:41.868
I'm sorry for lying.

00:03:41.868 --> 00:03:42.701
- It's okay.

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:43.534
- There's no more lying.

00:03:43.534 --> 00:03:44.517
- Are you sure?

00:03:44.517 --> 00:03:45.350
- Yeah!

00:03:45.792 --> 00:03:47.158
[Tania] How are you feeling?

00:03:47.158 --> 00:03:47.991
- Good!

00:03:48.670 --> 00:03:51.812
- Have the most romantic
holiday of your life.

00:03:51.812 --> 00:03:52.812
No pressure.

00:03:53.275 --> 00:03:54.204
- In Scotland.

00:03:54.204 --> 00:03:55.587
- I mean, the pressure's on me really.

00:03:55.587 --> 00:03:57.454
Have you missed vlogging?

00:03:57.454 --> 00:03:59.187
Isn't that part of the romance to capture

00:03:59.187 --> 00:04:01.028
every single intimate moment

00:04:01.028 --> 00:04:03.945
and share it with the entire world?

00:04:05.071 --> 00:04:06.238
[Upbeat Music]

00:04:14.936 --> 00:04:16.686
[Tania] That's Arran.

00:04:17.553 --> 00:04:19.705
Hopefully we can get
tickets to Arran tomorrow.

00:04:19.705 --> 00:04:21.753
It's a beautiful day in Scotland.

00:04:21.753 --> 00:04:25.289
And they're not quite used
to this amount of sun.

00:04:25.289 --> 00:04:27.537
We saw online that most
of the ferry tickets

00:04:27.537 --> 00:04:28.915
have already been booked out.

00:04:28.915 --> 00:04:30.657
So, it's going to be a bit shit

00:04:30.657 --> 00:04:34.740
if we don't manage to get
tickets to go to Arran.

00:04:34.971 --> 00:04:38.221
But I guess this is the
downside of not planning things

00:04:38.221 --> 00:04:40.333
and going to small country towns.

00:04:40.333 --> 00:04:42.176
Normally I'm, like, super organized.

00:04:42.176 --> 00:04:44.536
I overproduce everything in my life.

00:04:44.536 --> 00:04:47.210
Rachelle's always the
one that's teaching me

00:04:47.210 --> 00:04:48.690
to take it as it comes.

00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:50.074
If it doesn't work, it doesn't work.

00:04:50.074 --> 00:04:51.290
Her dad's going to come.

00:04:51.290 --> 00:04:53.738
So, it's not just going
to be the two of us,

00:04:53.738 --> 00:04:55.282
but we knew that going into it.

00:04:55.282 --> 00:04:56.962
Well, I knew that going into this.

00:04:56.962 --> 00:04:59.619
I'm kind of just at a
point in my life where

00:04:59.619 --> 00:05:01.475
these things mean a lot to me.

00:05:01.475 --> 00:05:03.258
I've heard that there's a castle there

00:05:03.258 --> 00:05:05.450
and some beautiful walks along the path.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:07.682
And everything is just a bus ride away.

00:05:07.682 --> 00:05:09.539
So, it should be easy getting around.

00:05:09.539 --> 00:05:12.300
I feel like I'm getting sicker, though.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:14.387
Hopefully it doesn't get any worse.

00:05:14.387 --> 00:05:15.637
[Wistful Music]

00:05:17.037 --> 00:05:21.787
Just woke up a little while
ago. She sounds healthy, too.

00:05:23.042 --> 00:05:25.792
Can't wait for an hour boat ride.

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:28.019
I was actually sick a couple days ago,

00:05:28.019 --> 00:05:29.523
and I've been trying to fight it.

00:05:29.523 --> 00:05:31.058
I wasn't even going to mention it,

00:05:31.058 --> 00:05:32.666
but it's come back with a vengeance.

00:05:32.666 --> 00:05:34.499
I'm sure I'll be fine.

00:05:38.469 --> 00:05:41.405
So, Rachelle, you've never been to Arran.

00:05:41.405 --> 00:05:42.880
- [Rachelle] I've never been to Arran.

00:05:42.880 --> 00:05:44.174
- I've never been.

00:05:44.174 --> 00:05:46.005
But it's been 40 years for you, Jim.

00:05:46.005 --> 00:05:46.861
- [Jim] Yes.

00:05:46.861 --> 00:05:47.694
- Wow.

00:05:48.301 --> 00:05:50.621
So, you've virtually never been either.

00:05:50.621 --> 00:05:52.371
- [Jim] That's right.

00:05:52.668 --> 00:05:55.001
- [Tania] What an adventure.

00:05:55.376 --> 00:05:56.876
We've got tickets!

00:05:57.640 --> 00:05:58.473
It's huge!

00:06:03.876 --> 00:06:07.718
It looks like we're walking
into another quarantine.

00:06:07.718 --> 00:06:09.051
[Cheerful Music]

00:06:14.721 --> 00:06:15.753
It's a beautiful day.

00:06:15.753 --> 00:06:18.674
It's really nice to be
hanging out with family!

00:06:18.674 --> 00:06:20.591
[Pleasant Fiddle Music]

00:06:47.453 --> 00:06:49.297
- [Rachelle] Do you like it, Dad?

00:06:49.297 --> 00:06:50.130
- Aye!

00:06:51.260 --> 00:06:54.102
- Shots! Shots! Shots!
Shots! Shots! Shots!

00:06:54.102 --> 00:06:56.230
It sucks that I feel so sick.

00:06:56.230 --> 00:07:00.007
I feel like just the smell
of the barley and malt

00:07:00.007 --> 00:07:01.719
just kind of hit my nose.

00:07:01.719 --> 00:07:04.351
And I don't know if you've
been in a distillery before,

00:07:04.351 --> 00:07:07.101
but imagine being in a perfumery.

00:07:07.159 --> 00:07:09.775
That is what it kind of smelled like.

00:07:09.775 --> 00:07:11.599
But now we're out in the fresh air.

00:07:11.599 --> 00:07:14.863
This is Rachelle's dad's
first whiskey tour.

00:07:14.863 --> 00:07:18.327
And now we're just going to
explore the island a little bit,

00:07:18.327 --> 00:07:19.872
see what we can find.

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:20.711
- How you feeling, Tania?

00:07:20.711 --> 00:07:22.247
- [Tania] It was so informative.

00:07:22.247 --> 00:07:24.998
I didn't know that the
shape of the still affected

00:07:24.998 --> 00:07:26.623
the chemical reduction

00:07:26.623 --> 00:07:29.022
and, therefore, the taste of whiskeys.

00:07:29.022 --> 00:07:31.279
What did you think of it, whiskey expert?

00:07:31.279 --> 00:07:32.950
- [Rachelle] I thought it was
good. It's a nice distillery.

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:33.783
Nice and modern.

00:07:33.783 --> 00:07:36.375
- Are you going to share your cake, or no?

00:07:36.375 --> 00:07:39.535
- [Tania] That's all your dad cares about.

00:07:39.535 --> 00:07:40.840
- [Rachelle] But can I do it!

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:43.460
- [Tania] We're about to
walk through a castle.

00:07:43.460 --> 00:07:44.877
[Peppy Pop Music]

00:08:00.603 --> 00:08:02.624
It's our last morning in Scotland.

00:08:02.624 --> 00:08:03.720
- Have you had a good time?

00:08:03.720 --> 00:08:06.040
- Yes. It's just been relaxing,

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:08.288
which is exactly what we need.

00:08:08.288 --> 00:08:09.400
- It was so good.

00:08:09.400 --> 00:08:11.058
- It was a bit ad hoc.

00:08:11.058 --> 00:08:11.891
- Yeah!

00:08:11.952 --> 00:08:14.613
But what we did see was
absolutely beautiful.

00:08:14.613 --> 00:08:18.329
- [Tania] Despite the nausea.
That just added some drama.

00:08:18.329 --> 00:08:20.023
It was nice for me to
hangout with your dad.

00:08:20.023 --> 00:08:22.855
What do you think you prefer
more in terms of dates?

00:08:22.855 --> 00:08:23.799
- [Rachelle] Oh, yeah.

00:08:23.799 --> 00:08:25.892
- [Tania] Kind of just
spontaneous, not well-planned?

00:08:25.892 --> 00:08:27.580
- [Rachelle] I prefer the outdoor stuff.

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:30.956
I prefer walking around on an
island, taking the boat out,

00:08:30.956 --> 00:08:32.389
than hanging out in a city.

00:08:32.389 --> 00:08:34.332
It's nice, and that's not to say Paris

00:08:34.332 --> 00:08:35.932
isn't a romantic place.

00:08:35.932 --> 00:08:37.508
But I think you can find it

00:08:37.508 --> 00:08:38.996
in different corners of the earth.

00:08:38.996 --> 00:08:41.380
- [Tania] Even though we were
with family the whole time?

00:08:41.380 --> 00:08:42.213
- Yeah!

00:08:44.417 --> 00:08:45.862
- Last summer, me and my
friends wanted to surprise

00:08:45.862 --> 00:08:47.568
our other friend for his birthday.

00:08:47.568 --> 00:08:49.120
So, we came up with this
whole elaborate plan

00:08:49.120 --> 00:08:51.576
that one of our friends lost
her purity ring at the beach.

00:08:51.576 --> 00:08:53.617
So, she and him went off to
the beach to look for it,

00:08:53.617 --> 00:08:55.513
while we stayed at the
house and decorated.

00:08:55.513 --> 00:08:57.784
When he came back, we all
screamed, "Happy birthday!"

00:08:57.784 --> 00:08:59.048
And it was so much fun.

00:08:59.048 --> 00:09:00.846
- I surprised my boyfriend
with an ultimate date.

00:09:00.846 --> 00:09:02.574
I took him to a PNC Pirates game,

00:09:02.574 --> 00:09:04.788
and afterwards we went
to a trivia wine night.

00:09:04.788 --> 00:09:06.613
And I kept it a secret the entire night.

00:09:06.613 --> 00:09:09.212
He only knew where we were
going once we got there.

00:09:09.212 --> 00:09:10.252
- I surprised one of my friends

00:09:10.252 --> 00:09:11.700
with a surprise birthday party.

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:12.940
I invited all of our friends.

00:09:12.940 --> 00:09:14.452
And we sat in my backyard.

00:09:14.452 --> 00:09:16.012
We had drinks. We swam in my pool.

00:09:16.012 --> 00:09:17.748
She still tells me that's
one of her favorite

00:09:17.748 --> 00:09:21.998
birthday memories, so it
makes it that much better.

00:09:32.027 --> 00:09:34.499
- Hey! Unsolved is on a new
channel. And now your part.

00:09:34.499 --> 00:09:35.332
- [Both] Subscribe here!

00:09:35.332 --> 00:09:36.915
- That was my part.

